6	 *             amber bulbs on the opening and on every ring lip). In the approved view these surfaces show the approved
7	 *             pixels (camera projection, unchanged); they fade to their own crisp 3D gold as the camera leaves that view.
8	 *  m04foam  — puffy 3D foam banks along both water edges (the painted white-lilac foam clusters), hidden in the approved
9	 *             view (the painting carries them there), shown once the camera has left it.
10	 *  m04bub   — iridescent soap bubbles floating in the tunnel air (camera-facing bubble discs), same visibility rule.
11	 *  m04arrow — the five glowing blue chevron arrows drawn crisp on the water (distance-field shape at the painted
12	 *             spacing) instead of the magnified painted arrow tile.
13	 *  m04wave  — the painted swirl water without the obvious repeat (two offset samples of the swirl tile blended by a
14	 *             slow world-anchored noise) and flowing down the slide.
15	 *  m04foam3 — (round 9, with m04foam + m04river) LOW soft foam hugging the river banks (heaps a third as tall, smaller
16	 *             puffs, wider gaps where the pink water shows), lavender / pink shaded like the painted foam.
17	 *  m04pink  — (round 9, with m04river) the broad pink / magenta swirl bands on both sides of the narrow cyan arrow lane.
18	 *  m04arr5  — (round 9, with m04river) the five glowing chevrons as painted: fat flat white-cyan bars nested one after
19	 *             the other ahead of Benny (about five in view at a time, the farther ones fading into the glow).
20	 *  m04mouth — (round 9, needs m04ring) the approved GOLD WASHER OPENING: the painted mouth ring (thick polished band,
21	 *             thin bright lips, dark groove) unwrapped from the approved pixels and straightened (tools/match04/mouth04.py
22	 *             -> tile_mouth.png) on a modeled mouth ring flush with the painted ring plane, mapped through the projector so
23	 *             the approach continues the approved view; its row of glowing bulbs (the painted hot spots on both lips,
24	 *             mouth04.json) drawn as crisp glowing bulbs at any distance.
25	 * Without `?match04=1` nothing here runs; without the sub-switches nothing here is built.
26	 */
27	import * as THREE from 'three';
28	import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/examples/jsm/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
29	import { PROJ05_INVERSE } from '../vfx/waterRibbon';
